<Base title="Research methodology"><div class="page-heading"><span class="kicker">HOW THE FILE IS BUILT</span><h1>Research methodology</h1><p>A reproducible approach to source checking, classification, and transparent uncertainty.</p></div><div class="prose"><h2>Scope</h2><p>The initial review window is 1 October through 21 November 2026. This is a curated starting file, not a comprehensive count of all media coverage. Only records with checked original publisher pages are public. Named research candidates are omitted until a relevant publication is confirmed.</p><h2>Metadata verification</h2><p>“Verified” means the original publisher page was checked for the headline, outlet, byline and publication date. It does not verify the story’s allegations. The tracker stores a canonical URL and source check date to support later review. Publisher update dates are shown only when confirmed.</p><h2>Claims and evidence</h2><p>Claim assessment is separate from article metadata. A claim may be documented, attributed, disputed or unverified. New entries default to unassessed. Summaries are original and short; readers should follow the publisher link for the reporting and its context.</p><h2>Editorial classification</h2><p>Tone describes the article’s overall framing toward Huang or NVIDIA: critical, neutral, supportive, or mixed. This is a judgment, not a measure of accuracy. Each article record includes a reason so readers can challenge the label. Article type distinguishes reported news from opinion and analysis.</p><h2>Funding disclosures</h2><p>Funding relationships require a public source, provider, recipient, type, and verification status. Ordinary employment is separate from project funding or fellowships. A relationship is never presented as proof of editorial direction without direct evidence.</p><h2>Corrections and challenges</h2><p>We record a publisher correction with its source and date when found. Readers can challenge metadata, classifications or summaries through the research team. The current build has an editor review queue but no public submission channel; contact details can be added when an editorial owner is appointed.</p><h2>Source standards</h2><p>Original publisher pages and primary disclosures take priority. Search results, prior conversations, and third-party summaries are leads, not publication evidence. The system does not bypass paywalls or reproduce full articles.</p></div></Base>
